Rand Wallet for Linux — the bare binary

This archive is the desktop app's executable on its own, for a distribution the .deb, the .rpm and
the AppImage do not fit. It is the same program: the shared wallet interface (the one the browser
extension shows) in the system webview, over the Rust wallet core.

It links against the system's webkit2gtk 4.1 and GTK 3, so install those first:

  Debian, Ubuntu    sudo apt install libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0
  Fedora            sudo dnf install webkit2gtk4.1
  Arch              sudo pacman -S webkit2gtk-4.1
  openSUSE          sudo zypper install libwebkit2gtk-4_1-0

Run it where it is:

  ./rand-wallet

Or install it for your user, with a launcher entry:

  install -Dm755 rand-wallet         ~/.local/bin/rand-wallet
  install -Dm644 rand-wallet.png     ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/rand-wallet.png
  install -Dm644 rand-wallet.desktop ~/.local/share/applications/rand-wallet.desktop

(~/.local/bin has to be on your PATH for the launcher entry to find it.)

The wallet keeps one file, ~/.config/RandWallet/wallet.json, readable by your user only. Sending
needs about 8 GiB of memory: the proof is made on this computer.

Check the download before you run it: SHA256SUMS is published with every release at
https://github.com/randprotocol/clients/releases

  sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing

